q(n,3,['options',3,'explanation'],'Link adaptation can depend on channel estimates and scheduler policy. The supplied trace specifically establishes RRC setup; it does not establish a special first-packet modulation rule.','Channel state/history can influence initial link adaptation.')
q(n,7,['options',2,'explanation'],'Correct. Expiration can disrupt an idle connection. Later traffic may be dropped, rejected or create another mapping, depending on the NAT and packet; continued TCP connectivity is not assured.','No universal later-packet discard after expiration.')
q(n,9,['options',3,'explanation'],'NAT64 is not restricted to port 443. Reachability still depends on supported protocols, mappings and policy; here the raw socket lacks a usable translated path.','Avoid claiming every port is necessarily translated.')
q(n,10,['options',3,'explanation'],'Keepalives can help detect some failures, but cannot migrate ordinary TCP across an endpoint-address change. Frequent probes add traffic and may increase energy use.','Energy cost is workload dependent and keepalive detection is conditional.')
